'=============================================================================
'
'  Stratus AS3935 Lightning Detection System
'  Logging the lightning records sent by the Raspberry Pi LDS
'
'  Property of METRON (PTY) LTD [Inteltronics]
'  Developer: L.J. Esterhuizen
'
'=============================================================================
' Site: QUAGGASKLIP
'
' Requires CR300 OS 6.0 or later. ComC2_Rx needs it. This unit is on 7.04.
'
' Record formats, 9600 baud 8N1, 3.3 V TTL, CR LF terminated:
'
'   L,<distance_km>,<energy>     lightning
'   H,<cpu_temp_c>,<rssi_dbm>    detector health, once a day
'
' distance_km is -1 when the sensor could not range the strike.
'
' Lightning is the only thing stored. H records are recognised and dropped, so
' health never reaches storage: that belongs to the admin panel, which is the
' system of record for whether a unit is alive. This logger therefore cannot tell
' a quiet sky from a dead detector. The panel answers that.
'
' EACH RECORD IS FOUND BY ITS FIRST LETTER, NOT BY READING THE WHOLE LINE.
' This matters. With BeginWord 0 the NBytes parameter becomes the count of bytes
' to keep before the EndWord, so passing 0 for both asks the logger to store
' nothing at all. It consumes each record and returns zero bytes, which looks
' exactly like a dead cable: BytesReturned stays 0, nothing parses, and no error
' is raised because the guard never runs. Keying on the letter, as Campbell's own
' example does, is what makes the read work. The letter is consumed as the
' BeginWord, so Dest receives ",40,1234567" and SplitStr takes it from there.
'
' WIRING. Two signals and a ground. BCM 14 is the Pi's hardware UART TX, brought
' out on mikroBUS socket 2 as the TX pin, so the Terminal 2 Click "TX" terminal
' is the one to use.
'
'   Pi BCM 14   Terminal 2 Click "TX"   ->  CR300  C2      records in
'   Pi BCM 19   header pin 35           ->  CR300  P_SW    strike pulse
'   Pi GND      Terminal 2 Click "GND"  ->  CR300  G       required
'
' The detector does not use the UART peripheral. It builds the 9600 baud waveform
' in software with pigpio, and the serial console has been taken off BCM 14 so
' the kernel does not fight it for the pin. The unit confirms the pin at startup:
' "Campbell UART TX enabled on GPIO 14 @ 9600 baud".
'
' C2 is the terminal this program opens for receive. Nothing listens on C1.
'
' Ground is not optional. Without it the receiver samples noise.
'
' Cable screen: land it at the CR300 end only, on signal ground. Cut it back and
' insulate it at the Pi end. The shield has no earth of its own, so grounding
' both ends would turn the screen into a ground loop conductor.
'
' Pi side, in /home/quaggasklip/lightning_config.json:
'   campbell_uart_enabled true, campbell_uart_tx_pin 14
'   pulse_mirror_enabled true, pulse_mirror_pin 19
' After editing: sudo systemctl restart lightning-detector
'
' The pulse mirror is an independent strike count taken straight off the sensor
' interrupt, so it does not depend on the serial line. PulseCountTotal and
' StrikeCount should track each other. Pulses ahead of serial means the serial
' path is dropping records; serial ahead of pulses means the pulse wire is at fault.
'=============================================================================

Const SCAN_MS = 200
Const CRLF = &H0D0A          ' EndWord for both reads
Const BW_LIGHTNING = &H4C    ' "L"
Const BW_HEALTH = &H48       ' "H"

Public LastDistanceKm As Float
Public LastEnergy As Long
Public StrikeCount As Long
Public StrikesToday As Long
Public ClosestTodayKm As Float
Public MaxEnergyToday As Long
Public PulseCountScan As Float
Public PulseCountTotal As Float
Public CountMismatch As Float

Public StrikeBody As String * 48
Public StrikeBytes As Float
Public HealthBody As String * 48
Public HealthBytes As Float
Public Parsed(2) As Float
Public ParseErrorCount As Long

' Live only, never sampled into a table, so no health reaches storage. It is a
' positive witness that the wire and ground are good after weeks with no
' lightning, which ParseErrorCount alone cannot tell you.
Public HealthRecordCount As Long

' Link diagnostics, also live only. SerialOpen returns False if the port refuses
' to open, and discarding that makes a refused port indistinguishable from a cut
' cable. SerialInChk counts bytes sitting in the buffer before anything consumes
' them and returns -1 if the port is not open. Bytes here with StrikeBytes and
' HealthBytes both 0 means data is arriving but not being framed.
Public SerialOpenOK As Boolean
Public BytesWaiting As Long

Dim EventRowWritten As Boolean

'=============================================================================
' DATA TABLES
'
' Distance, energy and the independent pulse count. Nothing else is stored.
' PulseCountTotal is IEEE4 because it is cumulative and FP2 stops at 7999,
' where it would saturate and also become indistinguishable from NAN.
'=============================================================================

DataTable (LightningEvents, True, -1)
  Sample (1, LastDistanceKm, FP2)
  Sample (1, LastEnergy, Long)
  Sample (1, PulseCountTotal, IEEE4)
EndTable

DataTable (LightningDaily, True, -1)
  DataInterval (0, 1, Day, 10)
  Sample (1, StrikesToday, Long)
  Sample (1, ClosestTodayKm, FP2)
  Sample (1, MaxEnergyToday, Long)
  Totalize (1, PulseCountScan, IEEE4, False)
EndTable

'=============================================================================
' PROGRAM
'=============================================================================

BeginProg
  ClosestTodayKm = NAN
  MaxEnergyToday = 0
  StrikesToday = 0

  SerialOpenOK = SerialOpen (ComC2_Rx, 9600, 0, 0, 256)
  SerialFlush (ComC2_Rx)

  Scan (SCAN_MS, mSec, 0, 0)

    EventRowWritten = False

    ' PConfig 2 = switch closure, POption 0 = counts.
    PulseCount (PulseCountScan, 1, P_SW, 2, 0, 1, 0)
    PulseCountTotal = PulseCountTotal + PulseCountScan

    ' Buffer depth before either read consumes it.
    BytesWaiting = SerialInChk (ComC2_Rx)

    ' Two reads on the one port, each keyed to a different first letter and each
    ' with its own read pointer, which is what option 110 selects. Without local
    ' pointers the two would compete for the same position in the buffer and one
    ' would swallow the other's records.
    SerialInRecord (ComC2_Rx, StrikeBody, BW_LIGHTNING, 0, CRLF, StrikeBytes, 110)
    SerialInRecord (ComC2_Rx, HealthBody, BW_HEALTH, 0, CRLF, HealthBytes, 110)

    If StrikeBytes > 0 Then

      ' SplitOption 0 is NUMERIC: it keeps + - . 0-9 E and treats everything else
      ' as a delimiter, so the leading comma of ",40,1234567" costs nothing and
      ' the two values land in Parsed(1) and Parsed(2).
      SplitStr (Parsed(1), StrikeBody, ",", 2, 0)

      ' x = x is false only for NAN, which catches a failed parse.
      If Parsed(1) = Parsed(1) AND Parsed(2) = Parsed(2) Then
        LastDistanceKm = Parsed(1)
        LastEnergy = Parsed(2)
        StrikeCount = StrikeCount + 1
        StrikesToday = StrikesToday + 1

        If LastEnergy > MaxEnergyToday Then MaxEnergyToday = LastEnergy

        ' -1 means unrangeable, so it is not a closest-of-day candidate.
        If LastDistanceKm >= 0 Then
          If ClosestTodayKm <> ClosestTodayKm Then
            ClosestTodayKm = LastDistanceKm
          ElseIf LastDistanceKm < ClosestTodayKm Then
            ClosestTodayKm = LastDistanceKm
          EndIf
        EndIf

        EventRowWritten = True
        CallTable LightningEvents
      Else
        ParseErrorCount = ParseErrorCount + 1
      EndIf
    EndIf

    ' Counted live, then dropped. Deliberately NOT added to ParseErrorCount:
    ' routine traffic accumulating in the fault counter would hide a missing
    ' ground or a baud mismatch.
    If HealthBytes > 0 Then
      HealthRecordCount = HealthRecordCount + 1
    EndIf

    CountMismatch = PulseCountTotal - StrikeCount

    ' A pulse with no serial record still deserves a row: the pulse is the
    ' hardware witness that the sensor fired. Gated on EventRowWritten so it
    ' cannot double up with the strike row above.
    If PulseCountScan > 0 And Not EventRowWritten Then
      CallTable LightningEvents
    EndIf

    ' Called every scan on purpose: Totalize accumulates once per CallTable, so
    ' gating this on IfTime would build the daily total from one sample a day.
    ' DataInterval decides when the row is written.
    CallTable LightningDaily

    ' Reset today's figures after the daily row is written above.
    If IfTime (0, 1, Day) Then
      StrikesToday = 0
      ClosestTodayKm = NAN
      MaxEnergyToday = 0
    EndIf

  NextScan
EndProg
